WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.350 --> 00:00:05.362
Hello, everyone! I'm Ms. Emma. Welcome to Online Grammar, level B two.

2
00:00:05.662 --> 00:00:09.246
Hi! I'm Visal. Let's learn together!

3
00:00:09.546 --> 00:00:16.285
Unit ten: Modal Verbs in the Past. Today you will talk about past deductions, regrets and criticism.

4
00:00:16.585 --> 00:00:19.260
Here is our lesson map. Let's start!

5
00:00:20.200 --> 00:00:23.758
Part one: words. You will learn eight new words.

6
00:00:24.617 --> 00:00:25.641
Must have.

7
00:00:26.650 --> 00:00:29.462
Must have means a strong deduction about the past.

8
00:00:30.050 --> 00:00:31.411
He must have left.

9
00:00:32.017 --> 00:00:34.739
Your turn. Say: Must have.

10
00:00:37.600 --> 00:00:38.659
Must have.

11
00:00:39.417 --> 00:00:40.360
Might have.

12
00:00:41.350 --> 00:00:44.011
Might have means a weak possibility in the past.

13
00:00:44.617 --> 00:00:45.885
She might have forgotten.

14
00:00:46.483 --> 00:00:48.869
Your turn. Say: Might have.

15
00:00:51.733 --> 00:00:52.792
Might have.

16
00:00:53.550 --> 00:00:54.319
Could have.

17
00:00:55.317 --> 00:00:58.442
Could have means a past possibility or missed chance.

18
00:00:59.050 --> 00:01:00.109
I could have won.

19
00:01:00.717 --> 00:01:03.764
Your turn. Say: Could have.

20
00:01:06.600 --> 00:01:07.624
Could have.

21
00:01:08.383 --> 00:01:09.512
Should have.

22
00:01:10.517 --> 00:01:13.608
Should have means a criticism or regret about the past.

23
00:01:14.217 --> 00:01:15.357
I should have called.

24
00:01:15.950 --> 00:01:18.939
Your turn. Say: Should have.

25
00:01:21.800 --> 00:01:22.987
Should have.

26
00:01:23.750 --> 00:01:24.995
Past deduction.

27
00:01:25.983 --> 00:01:29.237
Past deduction means a conclusion about a past event.

28
00:01:29.850 --> 00:01:31.687
A logical past deduction.

29
00:01:32.283 --> 00:01:35.412
Your turn. Say: Past deduction.

30
00:01:38.267 --> 00:01:39.813
Past deduction.

31
00:01:40.550 --> 00:01:41.435
Regret.

32
00:01:42.450 --> 00:01:44.682
Regret means sadness about the past.

33
00:01:45.283 --> 00:01:46.621
I feel regret.

34
00:01:47.217 --> 00:01:50.182
Your turn. Say: Regret.

35
00:01:53.033 --> 00:01:54.104
Regret.

36
00:01:54.850 --> 00:01:56.652
Possibility in the past.

37
00:01:57.650 --> 00:02:00.799
Possibility in the past means something that may have happened.

38
00:02:01.383 --> 00:02:03.360
A possibility in the past.

39
00:02:03.950 --> 00:02:07.729
Your turn. Say: Possibility in the past.

40
00:02:10.567 --> 00:02:12.775
Possibility in the past.

41
00:02:13.517 --> 00:02:14.471
Certainty.

42
00:02:15.483 --> 00:02:17.738
Certainty means complete confidence.

43
00:02:18.350 --> 00:02:19.955
I speak with certainty.

44
00:02:20.550 --> 00:02:23.353
Your turn. Say: Certainty.

45
00:02:26.200 --> 00:02:27.073
Certainty.

46
00:02:27.867 --> 00:02:31.343
Part two: dialogue. Let's listen to a conversation.

47
00:02:32.183 --> 00:02:34.949
Visal, tell me something you should have done differently.

48
00:02:36.050 --> 00:02:43.776
I should have studied more for the exam. Should have plus a past participle expresses regret or criticism about the past.

49
00:02:44.883 --> 00:02:46.256
What about deduction?

50
00:02:47.350 --> 00:02:57.226
She must have missed the bus means I am almost sure. She might have forgotten means it is possible. He can't have seen us means I am almost sure he did not.

51
00:02:58.317 --> 00:02:59.457
And could have?

52
00:03:00.550 --> 00:03:10.540
Could have shows a past possibility or a missed chance: I could have won, but I made a mistake. Needn't have means it was unnecessary.

53
00:03:11.700 --> 00:03:13.258
Part three: grammar.

54
00:03:14.117 --> 00:03:17.544
Grammar focus: Modal plus have plus past participle.

55
00:03:17.844 --> 00:03:19.147
Look at the pattern.

56
00:03:19.850 --> 00:03:21.896
I should have studied more for the exam.

57
00:03:22.783 --> 00:03:24.400
She must have missed the bus.

58
00:03:25.283 --> 00:03:26.969
He can't have seen us.

59
00:03:27.933 --> 00:03:35.897
Must have = sure. Might / could have = possible. Can't have = sure it didn't happen. Should have = regret or criticism.

60
00:03:36.650 --> 00:03:39.883
Be careful! Don't say: I should called you.

61
00:03:41.833 --> 00:03:43.496
Say: I should have called you.

62
00:03:43.796 --> 00:03:45.680
Use should have + participle.

63
00:03:46.467 --> 00:03:49.049
Part four: reading. Read and listen.

64
00:03:49.833 --> 00:03:50.892
Looking Back.

65
00:03:51.192 --> 00:03:53.668
I should have studied more for the exam last week.

66
00:03:54.667 --> 00:03:56.701
The teacher must have been disappointed.

67
00:03:57.700 --> 00:03:59.769
I could have achieved a better result.

68
00:04:00.767 --> 00:04:03.532
My friend might have forgotten to tell me about the change.

69
00:04:04.533 --> 00:04:06.719
It was a regret, but I learned from it.

70
00:04:07.833 --> 00:04:11.812
Part five: quiz. Five questions. Are you ready?

71
00:04:12.650 --> 00:04:15.233
She isn't here. She blank missed the bus.

72
00:04:15.533 --> 00:04:19.488
A, must have. B, should have. C, would.

73
00:04:23.033 --> 00:04:24.952
The answer is A: must have.

74
00:04:26.117 --> 00:04:29.164
I blank called you, but I forgot. (regret)

75
00:04:29.464 --> 00:04:33.106
A, should have. B, must have. C, might.

76
00:04:36.667 --> 00:04:38.922
The answer is A: should have.

77
00:04:40.083 --> 00:04:42.176
He blank been there; he was abroad.

78
00:04:42.476 --> 00:04:46.396
A, must have. B, can't have. C, should have.

79
00:04:49.933 --> 00:04:52.026
The answer is B: can't have.

80
00:04:53.183 --> 00:04:54.904
Which shows a missed chance?

81
00:04:55.204 --> 00:04:59.287
A, I will win.. B, I won.. C, I could have won..

82
00:05:02.833 --> 00:05:05.135
The answer is C: I could have won..

83
00:05:06.283 --> 00:05:08.887
According to the reading, what was the writer's regret?

84
00:05:09.187 --> 00:05:13.595
A, not studying enough. B, missing a bus. C, losing a book.

85
00:05:17.133 --> 00:05:19.864
The answer is A: not studying enough.

86
00:05:21.067 --> 00:05:24.543
Part six: speaking. It's your turn to talk.

87
00:05:25.383 --> 00:05:29.473
Write a sentence guessing what happened in the past using a modal + have.

88
00:05:38.283 --> 00:05:39.679
Now listen to Visal.

89
00:05:39.979 --> 00:05:49.112
I should have started revising earlier. My teacher must have noticed that I was nervous. I might have got a better grade, but I learned to plan my time.

90
00:05:49.412 --> 00:05:51.122
Excellent answer, Visal!

91
00:05:52.017 --> 00:05:57.293
Great work! Now you can use eight new words and modal plus have plus past participle.

92
00:05:57.593 --> 00:06:01.546
Today's value is reflection. Think about what you learned and how you grew.

93
00:06:01.846 --> 00:06:04.324
See you in Unit eleven. Goodbye!

94
00:06:04.624 --> 00:06:07.276
Thank you, Ms. Emma! Bye, everyone!

